# The groom and its strand atlas are BUILD OUTPUT, exactly like assets/wardrobe/*/*.glb and
# assets/figures/*.glb, and for the same reason: they come out of headless Blender in about ten
# seconds and re-derive byte-identically from the seed in manifest.json.
#
#   blender --background --python tools/figure-pipeline/build_figure.py --python-exit-code 1 -- \
#       --gender 0.5 --output assets/figures/figure_g050.glb --hair bob01
#
# The manifest is NOT build output. It is authored, it is what the build, the runtime and
# verify_glb.mjs all read the groom's alphaMode, cutoff, bone and map names from, and it is
# committed.
# ⚠️ THE POLICY ABOVE IS REVERSED AND THE REASONING IS KEPT BECAUSE IT IS STILL CORRECT ABOUT THE
# BUILD. The groom really is regenerable in about ten seconds. What changed is who is reading this
# repository: a public consumer has no Blender and no MPFB2, so a regenerable asset they cannot
# regenerate is a missing asset. Committed through git-LFS instead. See .gitattributes.
